hadiths[125]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1629","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I saw in a dream that people were being presented before me and they were wearing shirts. Some of their shirts reached up to their chests, and some were even shorter than that. Then 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) appeared, and he was wearing such a long shirt that it was dragging on the ground. The people asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the interpretation of this? He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Religion."
"1630","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: I was sleeping and in my sleep a bowl was brought before me in which there was milk. I drank from it until freshness and satisfaction began to come out from my fingernails. Then what was left, I gave to Umar bin Khattab. The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is its interpretation?"" He (peace be upon him) said: Its interpretation is knowledge."
"1631","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: I was asleep, and I saw myself at a well upon which there was a bucket. So I drew water from that bucket as much as Allah willed. Then the son of Abu Quhafa, that is, Siddiq Akbar (Abu Bakr), took it and drew one or two buckets, and there was some weakness in his drawing—may Allah forgive him. Then that bucket became a large bucket, and Umar bin Khattab took it, and I have never seen a strong chief among the people who drew water as Umar did. He drew so much water that the people watered their camels and took them to their resting places. (__QUR_N__, __XREF_N__, __REF_N__) (The scholars have stated that in this dream there is a representation and glad tidings of the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Umar after you, and a prophecy of the circumstances.)"
"1632","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: I was sleeping and I saw myself in Paradise. There, a woman was performing ablution in the corner of a palace. I asked, ""Whose palace is this?"" (The angels) replied, ""It is Umar bin Khattab's."" Upon hearing this, I remembered his sense of honor, so I turned away and left. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) heard this, he began to weep, and we were all in the gathering with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""May my parents be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! Would I be jealous of you?"""
"1633","The conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), says that Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to enter, and at that time, there were women of the Quraysh sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), talking to him, speaking a lot, and their voices were raised. When Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) called out, they got up and ran to hide. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) permission to enter, and he (the Prophet) was smiling. Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “May Allah always keep you smiling, O Messenger of Allah!” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “I was amazed at these women who were sitting with me; as soon as they heard your voice, they rushed into veils.” Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! They should fear you more.” Then he said to the women, “O enemies of yourselves! You fear me but do not fear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?” They replied, “Yes, you are harsher and more stern than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, whenever Satan meets you on a path, he leaves that path and takes another.”"
"1634","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Among the previous nations before you, there used to be people who were ""Muhaddath"" (whose opinions were correct, whose intuition was right, or to whom angels would inspire). If there is anyone like that in my Ummah, it would be Umar ibn al-Khattab. Ibn Wahb said that the meaning of ""Muhaddathun"" is ""those who are inspired."""
"1635","‘Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that’ Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was in agreement with my Lord in three matters. One was performing prayer at the Station of Ibrahim (when I suggested, O Messenger of Allah! Make this place a place of prayer, and it was revealed in the Qur’an as such), the second was regarding the veiling of women, and the third was regarding the captives of Badr."
"1636","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` when Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul, the well-known hypocrite, died, his son Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), son of Abdullah bin Ubayy, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and requested, ""O Messenger of Allah, please give your shirt for my father's shroud."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave it. Then he said, ""Please lead the funeral prayer for him."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up to pray over him. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) held onto the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Will you pray over him even though Allah has forbidden you to pray over him?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Allah has given me the choice: 'Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them' (At-Tawbah: 80). So I will ask more than seventy times."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Indeed, he was a hypocrite."" Yet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed over him. Then the verse was revealed: ""Do not ever pray over any of them who dies, nor stand at his grave"" (At-Tawbah: 84). (Thus, Allah approved the opinion of Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him.)"
"1637","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was lying in his house with his thighs or shins uncovered, when suddenly Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) asked for permission to enter. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted him permission in that state and continued talking with him. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked for permission, and he was also allowed in the same state, and they continued talking. Then Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) asked for permission, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sat up and arranged his clothes. Then he came in and they talked. (The narrator Muhammad says: I do not say that the coming of all three happened on the same day.) When he left, Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came, you did not pay any attention, then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came, and you still did not pay any attention, but when Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) came, you sat up and arranged your clothes. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Should I not feel shy before a man before whom even the angels feel shy?"
"1638","Saeed bin Musayyib says that Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that he performed ablution in his house, then went out. Abu Musa says: I said, ""Today I will not leave the company of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) all day; I will stay with him."" He says: Then I came to the mosque and inquired about the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The people said that he had gone out in that direction. So I followed in the footsteps of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and kept asking people about him. While walking, I found out that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had gone into a garden at the place of Aris. I sat near the door, which was made of palm branches, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished relieving himself and had performed ablution, then I walked towards him. I saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting on the edge of the well of Aris, with both his shins uncovered and dangling in the well. So I greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and then returned to sit near the door. I said (to myself): Today I will be the doorkeeper/guard of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Meanwhile, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came and pushed the door. I asked, ""Who is it?"" He said, ""Abu Bakr."" I said, ""Wait a moment."" Then I went and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Abu Bakr seeks permission to enter."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Let him in and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" I came and told Abu Bakr, ""Enter, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has given you glad tidings of Paradise."" So Abu Bakr entered and sat on the right side of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the same edge, with both his legs dangling and his shins uncovered, just as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting. I returned and sat down again, and I had left my brother (Amir) performing ablution at home. I said, ""If Allah wills good for so-and-so (i.e., my brother), He will bring him here."" Meanwhile (what do I see but) someone started shaking the door. I asked, ""Who is it?"" The reply came, ""Umar bin Khattab."" I said, ""Wait."" Then I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), greeted him, and said, ""Umar bin Khattab seeks permission to enter."" He said, ""Let him in and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" So I went and said, ""Enter, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has given you glad tidings of Paradise."" So he also entered and sat on the left side of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the same edge, and both his legs were dangling in the well. Then I returned and sat (at the door). I said, ""If Allah wills good for so-and-so (Amir), He will bring him here."" Meanwhile, another man shook the door. I said, ""Who is it?"" He replied, ""Uthman bin Affan."" I said, ""Wait."" Then I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him, so he said, ""Let him in and give him glad tidings of Paradise, but he will be afflicted with a calamity."" I came and said to him, ""Enter, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has given you glad tidings of Paradise, but with a trial that will befall you."" So he also entered and saw that a part of the edge was filled, so he sat on the other side, facing the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Shareek said that Saeed bin Musayyib said: I derived from this hadith that their graves would also be in this order. (And so it happened that Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) did not find a place in that chamber, so he was buried in Baqi' in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him))."
"1639","‘The conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) as his deputy (in Madinah) on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk. So he (Ali) said, “O Messenger of Allah! Are you leaving me among women and children?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Are you not pleased that your status with me is like that of Harun (Aaron) with Musa (Moses), except that there is no prophet after me?”"
"1640","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the battle of Khaybar: “I will give this flag to the person at whose hand Allah will grant victory, and he loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah and His Messenger love him.” Then the people spent the whole night discussing who would be given this honor by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When morning came, everyone went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hoping that the flag would be given to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Where is Ali bin Abi Talib?” The people replied, “O Messenger of Allah! His eyes are sore.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him, applied his saliva to his eyes, and prayed for him, so he was completely cured as if he had no ailment. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him the flag. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted, “O Messenger of Allah! Shall I fight them until they become like us (i.e., Muslims)?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Proceed gently until you reach their ground, then invite them to Islam and inform them of what is obligatory upon them from the rights of Allah. By Allah, if Allah guides a single person through you, it is better for you than red camels.”"
"1641","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a man from the descendants of Marwan became the ruler in Madinah, he summoned Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) and ordered him to curse Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) refused, so the man said, “If you refuse to curse, then say: May Allah’s curse be upon Abu Turab.” Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) loved no name more than Abu Turab, and he would be pleased with anyone who called him by this name.” The man said, “Tell me the story of why he was called Abu Turab.” Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the house of Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) and did not find Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) at home. He (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ‘Where is your cousin?’ She replied, ‘There was something between me and him, and he got angry and left, and he did not sleep here.’ The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to a man, ‘See where he is.’ The man came and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah! Ali is sleeping in the mosque.’ The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who was lying down, and his cloak had slipped from his side and dust had gotten on his body. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) began to wipe off the dust and said, ‘O Abu Turab! Get up. O Abu Turab! Get up.’"
"1642","Abu Uthman says: In those days when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to fight (the disbelievers), there were some days when no one remained with him except Sayyiduna Talha and Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1643","‘Muhammad bin Munkadir narrates from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) encouraged the people to strive in jihad on the day of the Trench. Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) responded, “I am present and ready.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called again, and Sayyiduna Zubair was the one who responded. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called again, and Sayyiduna Zubair was the one who responded. Finally, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Every prophet has a special companion, and my special companion is Zubair.”"
"1644","Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) says: On the day of the Trench, Umar bin Abi Salamah and I were with the women in the fortress of Hassan bin Thabit. Sometimes he would bend down for me to look, and sometimes I would bend down for him to look. I recognized my father at that time when he went out towards Banu Qurayza armed and mounted on a horse. Later, I mentioned this to my father, and he said, ""Son, did you see me?"" I said, ""Yes."" He said, ""By Allah, on that day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) combined his parents for me and said, 'May my parents be sacrificed for you.'"""
"1645","‘Sayyiduna Urwah bin Zubair says that’ Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said to me: By Allah, both your fathers (that is, Zubair and Abu Bakr) are among those mentioned in this verse, that is, “those who obeyed Allah and His Messenger even after being wounded.” (Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, was Urwah’s maternal grandfather and Sayyiduna Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him, was his father. But a grandfather is also called a father.) And in another narration it is: “That is, Abu Bakr and Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both).”"
"1646","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the mountain of Hira. The rock of the mountain shook, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Be still, O Hira! There is none upon you except a Prophet, a Siddiq, or a martyr."" And with him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, Umar, Ali, Uthman, Talhah, and Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them). (The Prophet was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) himself, the Siddiq was Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and the rest were all martyred, killed unjustly, including Sayyiduna Talhah and Zubair.)"
"1647","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that one night (while returning from a battle) on the way to Madinah, the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) opened and he could not sleep, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I wish that someone from among my companions, a fortunate one, would guard me throughout the night.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that just then we heard the sound of weapons, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Who is it?” A voice replied: “O Messenger of Allah! It is Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Why have you come?” He replied: “I felt fear for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) within myself, so I have come to guard you.” Thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for him and then slept."
"1648","Sayyiduna Amir bin Sa’d narrates from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gathered his parents for him on the day of Uhud. Sayyiduna Sa’d, may Allah be pleased with him, said that there was a man among the polytheists who had caused great harm to many Muslims (i.e., he had martyred many Muslims). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “O Sa’d, shoot arrows, may my parents be sacrificed for you.” I took out an arrow for him which did not have a tip; it struck his rib and he (the polytheist) fell down, and his private parts became exposed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) laughed upon seeing this, to the extent that I saw his blessed teeth."
"1649","‘Mus’ab bin Sa’d narrates from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that’ several verses of the Qur’an were revealed about him. He says that his mother had sworn that she would never speak to him until he left his religion (i.e., Islam). And she would neither eat nor drink. She said, “Allah Almighty has commanded you to obey your parents, and I am your mother, and I command you to do this.” Then for three days she remained like this, eating and drinking nothing, until she fainted. Finally, one of her sons, whose name was ‘Ammarah, stood up and gave her water to drink. Then she began to curse Sayyiduna Sa’d, so Allah the Exalted revealed these verses in the Noble Qur’an: “And We have enjoined upon man [care] for his parents” (__QUR_N__) (Al-‘Ankabut: 8), “But if they strive to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them (i.e., do not commit shirk), but accompany them in this world with appropriate kindness” (__QUR_N__) (Luqman: 5). And once, a large amount of war booty came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and among it was a sword. I took it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Please give me this sword as a gift, as you know my situation.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Put it back where you took it from.” I went and intended to put it back in the pile of war booty, but my heart reproached me, so I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “Please give me this sword.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sternly said, “Put it back where you took it from.” Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: “They ask you about the spoils of war” (__QUR_N__) (Al-Anfal: 1). Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I became ill, so I sent for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He came, and I said, “Allow me to distribute my wealth to whomever I wish.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not permit it. I said, “Then may I give away half my wealth?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not permit it. I said, “Then may I give away a third of my wealth?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. Then it was established that giving away a third of one’s wealth is permissible. Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Once I went to some people among the Ansar and Muhajirin, and they said, “Come, we will give you food and wine,” and at that time wine had not yet been forbidden. I went with them to a garden, where the meat of a camel’s head was roasted, and a waterskin of wine was placed. I ate the meat and drank the wine with them. There, the topic of the Muhajirin and Ansar came up, so I said, “The Muhajirin are better than the Ansar.” A man took a bone from the jaw and struck me with it, injuring my nose. I reported this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse because of me: “Wine, gambling, idols, and divining arrows are all filth and the work of Satan” (__QUR_N__) (Al-Ma’idah: 90)."
"1650","Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were six men with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The polytheists said, “Drive these people away from you; they will not dare to confront us.” Among those people were myself, Ibn Mas’ud, a man from Hudhail, Bilal, and two others whose names I do not mention. Whatever Allah willed came to your heart, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke to himself inwardly. Then Allah revealed this verse: “Do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His pleasure.” (__QUR_6:52__)"
"1651","`Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the people of Najran came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Send to us a trustworthy person."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I will surely send to you a trustworthy person. Indeed, he is trustworthy, indeed, he is trustworthy."" The narrator said that the people waited to see whom the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would send, and then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"1652","Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I led the white mule on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) were riding, until I brought them to the Prophet’s chamber. One of these grandsons was in front of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the other was behind him."
"1653","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at a certain time during the day, and neither did he speak to me nor did I speak to him (that is, we walked in silence), until we reached the market of Banu Qaynuqa. Then he returned and came to the house of Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) and asked, ""Is the child here? Is the child here?""—meaning he was asking about Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him). We thought that his mother had kept him back to bathe him, clean him, and put a fragrant necklace on him, but shortly after, he came running, and the two embraced each other (that is, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and Sayyiduna Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! I love him, so You love him, and love the one who loves him."""
"1654","Narrated from Sayyiduna Miswar bin Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a marriage proposal to the daughter of Abu Jahl, while the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), was in his marriage. When Sayyidah Fatimah az-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) heard this news, she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""People say about you that you do not get angry for the sake of your daughters, and here is Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who is going to marry the daughter of Abu Jahl."" Sayyiduna Miswar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the testimony of faith and then said, ""I married my daughter (Sayyidah Zaynab, may Allah be pleased with her) to Abul-As ibn Rabi', and he spoke to me truthfully. And Fatimah bint Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is a part of my flesh, and I dislike that people put her to trial (meaning, if Ali marries again, perhaps Fatimah, out of jealousy, might say something against her husband or disobey him and become sinful). By Allah! The daughter of the Messenger of Allah and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will not be together with one man."" Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) abandoned the proposal (i.e., he gave up the intention to marry the daughter of Abu Jahl)."
"1655","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that all the pure wives (may Allah be pleased with them) of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were with him (during his illness), there was no wife who was not present, when suddenly Sayyida Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) came, and she walked exactly as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to walk. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw her, he said, “Welcome,” and said, “Welcome, my daughter.” Then he made her sit on his right or left side, and whispered something in her ear, so she wept greatly. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw her in this state, he again whispered something in her ear, so she laughed. I said to her, “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has especially confided something to you, yet you weep.” When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, I asked her, “What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say to you?” She replied, “I am not one to disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, I made her swear by the right I had over her and said, “Tell me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to you.” She said, “Now, indeed, I will tell you. The first time, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) whispered in my ear that Jibreel (peace be upon him) used to review the Qur’an with me once every year or twice, and this year he reviewed it twice, and I think that my (time to depart from this world) is near. So fear Allah and be patient, for I am the best forerunner for you. Hearing this, I began to weep as you saw. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw me weeping, he again whispered to me and said, ‘O Fatimah! Are you not pleased that you will be the leader of the women of the believers or the women of this Ummah?’ Hearing this, I laughed as you saw.”"
"1656","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the morning and he was wrapped in a cloak on which there were designs of camel saddles or pots. In the meantime, our master Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him under the cloak. Then our master Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so he was also included in it. Then Lady Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) came, so she was also included with them. Then our master Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so he was also included, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah only wishes to remove impurity from you, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.” (Al-Ahzab: 33). (This does not mean that the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are not his household, as is the belief of the Shia; rather, in reality, the household primarily refers to the wives, as the context of the verse also indicates. Along with them, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also included Ali, Fatimah, and Hasan and Husain (may Allah be pleased with them all).)"
"1657","Yazid bin Hayan says: I, Husain bin Sabrah, and Umar bin Muslim went to Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him). When we sat with him, Husain said, “O Zaid! You have attained great virtue. You saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), heard his hadith, participated in jihad with him, and prayed with him. You have earned much reward. Narrate to us some hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” He said, “O my nephew! I have grown very old and much time has passed, and some things which I used to remember from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) I have forgotten. Accept whatever I narrate, and do not trouble me for what I do not narrate.” Then Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up one day to deliver a sermon at a place called Khumm, between Makkah and Madinah, at the water of Khumm. He praised Allah and glorified Him, and gave admonition and advice. Then he said, “After this, O people! I am a human being. Soon the messenger of my Lord (the angel of death) will come to me and I will accept (his call). I am leaving among you two weighty things. The first is the Book of Allah, in which is guidance and light. So hold fast to the Book of Allah and adhere to it firmly.” Thus, he encouraged adherence to the Book of Allah. Then he said, “The second thing is my Ahl al-Bayt (household). I remind you of Allah regarding my Ahl al-Bayt, I remind you of Allah regarding my Ahl al-Bayt, I remind you of Allah regarding my Ahl al-Bayt,” three times. Husain asked, “O Zaid! Who are the Ahl al-Bayt of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)? Are his noble wives not among the Ahl al-Bayt?” Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “The noble wives are also among the Ahl al-Bayt, but the Ahl al-Bayt are those upon whom zakat is forbidden.” Husain asked, “Who are they?” Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “They are the descendants of Ali, Aqeel, Ja’far, and Abbas.” Husain asked, “Is charity forbidden for all of them?” Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Yes.”"
"1658","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I saw you in a dream for three nights, when an angel brought you to me in a piece of white silk and said to me, ""This is your wife."" I uncovered your face and it was you. I said, ""If this dream is from Allah, then it will happen as such (i.e., this woman will be given to me if there is no other interpretation of this dream)."""
"1659","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me, “I know when you are pleased with me and when you are displeased with me.” I asked, “How do you know that?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “When you are pleased, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him),’ and when you are angry, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Ibrahim (peace be upon him).’” I said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! I only leave your name (when I am angry with you).” (The anger of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) was only due to the jealousy that is excused for women, and it was only outward; in her heart, she was never displeased with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).)"
"1660","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she used to play with dolls in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). She said that her friends would come and, upon seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), would hide (out of shyness and fear), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would send them to her."
"1661","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that people used to wait for my turn, and on the day of my turn, they would send gifts so that the Prophet (peace be upon him) would be pleased."
"1662","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the pure wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his daughter, Sayyida Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her), to him. She asked for permission, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lying with me under my sheet. When he granted permission, she said, “O Messenger of Allah! Your wives have sent me to you; they wish that you be just with the daughter of Abu Quhafah (meaning, that you love them as much as you love her. And this matter was not optional, and in all other matters you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were just).” And I remained silent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “O daughter! Do you not want what I want?” She replied, “O Messenger of Allah! I only want what you want.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Then love Aisha.” Upon hearing this, Fatimah got up and went to the wives of the Prophet and conveyed to them what she had said and what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said. They said, “We think you will not be of any help to us, so go again to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say that his wives seek justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah (Abu Quhafah was the father of our master Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), so he was Aisha’s grandfather, and it is permissible to attribute to the grandfather).” Sayyida Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “By Allah! I will never speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again regarding Aisha’s matter.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that finally, the wives of the Prophet sent Umm al-Mu’minin Zaynab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in rank she was equal to me before him. I have not seen any woman more religious, more God-fearing, more truthful in speech, more upholding of kinship, and more charitable than her, nor any woman who strove harder in Allah’s cause and in charity than her, except that she had a quick temper (i.e., she would get angry), but she would quickly calm down, reconcile, and feel remorse. She sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he granted it while he was still in my sheet, just as he was when Sayyida Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) had come. She said, “O Messenger of Allah! Your wives seek justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah.” Then she turned to me and spoke harshly, and I was watching the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to see if he would permit me to respond or not, until I realized that he would not mind if I replied. Then I responded to her and soon overcame her or rendered her speechless. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said, “She is the daughter of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) (not just any woman who would be subdued by you).”"
"1663","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to ask during his illness, ""Where will I be today? Where will I be tomorrow?"" thinking that his turn (to stay with her) was still delayed. Then, on my day, Allah the Exalted called him (to Himself) while his blessed head was resting on my chest and throat."
"1664","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying before his death, while he was leaning on her chest. She listened closely and he (peace and blessings be upon him) was saying: ""O Allah! Forgive me, have mercy on me, and join me with the highest companions."""
"1665","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say in his state of health that no prophet passes away until he has seen his place in Paradise and has been given the choice to depart from this world. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that when the time of the Messenger of Allah’s (peace and blessings be upon him) death came, his head was on my thigh. He (peace and blessings be upon him) remained unconscious for a while, then regained consciousness and fixed his gaze towards the ceiling and said, “O Allah! With the highest companions (meaning with the prophets who reside in the highest ‘Illiyyin).” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that at that moment I realized that now he (peace and blessings be upon him) would not choose us, and I remembered the hadith which he (peace and blessings be upon him) had said in his state of health, that no prophet passes away until he has seen his place in Paradise and has been given the choice (between remaining in this world and the Hereafter). Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that this was the last statement the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made: “O Allah! With the highest companions.”"
"1666","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. Once, the lot fell upon me and Umm al-Mu’minin Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her), and both of us set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When he traveled at night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would walk alongside Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), conversing with her as they went. Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) said to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), “Tonight, you ride my camel and I will ride yours; you will see what you have not seen, and I will see what I have not seen.” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) agreed. So, she rode Hafsa’s camel and Hafsa rode hers. At night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the camel of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), on which Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) was riding. He greeted her and walked alongside her until they halted at the destination. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) did not find the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with her that night, so she became jealous. When she dismounted, she put her feet in the idhkhir grass and said, “O Allah! Set a scorpion or a snake upon me that it may bite me. He is Your Messenger; I cannot say anything to him.”"
"1667","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Many men have attained perfection, but among women none attained perfection except Maryam bint ‘Imran and Asiyah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of Pharaoh. And the superiority of ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) over other women is like the superiority of tharid over other foods."
"1668","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aisha! This is Jibreel (peace be upon him); he is conveying greetings of peace to you."" I replied, ""(And peace and the mercy of Allah be upon him)."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to see things which I did not see."
"1669","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that eleven women sat together and all of them made a pact and promise that they would not conceal anything about their husbands. The first woman said: My husband is like the meat of a lean camel placed on the top of a difficult-to-climb mountain. There is no clear path to reach it so that someone may climb, nor is the meat fat so that it may be brought down. The second woman said: I cannot spread news about my husband; I fear that if I describe him, I will not be able to fully express it, for he has many apparent and hidden faults. (And some have interpreted this to mean: I fear that if I describe him, I will have to leave him, i.e., he will get angry and divorce me, and I will have to leave him.) The third woman said: My husband is tall and foolish; if I mention his faults, he will divorce me, and if I remain silent, I will remain suspended (i.e., I will neither enjoy the pleasures of marriage nor be completely deprived). The fourth said: My husband is like the night of Tihamah (Hijaz and Mecca)—neither hot nor cold (i.e., he is moderate in temperament), there is neither fear nor sorrow (this is praise, meaning his character is excellent and he is not annoyed by my company). The fifth woman said: When my husband comes home, he is like a cheetah (i.e., he lies down and sleeps and does not bother anyone), and when he goes out, he is like a lion. And whatever wealth and goods he leaves at home, he does not inquire about them. The sixth woman said: If my husband eats, he finishes everything, and if he drinks, he leaves nothing even at the bottom, and when he lies down, he wraps himself up, and he does not put his hand on me to recognize my pain or sorrow (this is also satire, meaning he is like an ox, good for nothing except eating and drinking, and does not care about his wife). The seventh woman said: My husband is impotent or wicked, extremely foolish, does not know how to speak, and has all the faults of the world in him. He is so cruel that he may break your head or your hand, or twist both your head and hand. The eighth woman said: My husband, in fragrance, is like zarnab (a fragrant grass), and to the touch, soft like a rabbit (this is praise, meaning both his outward and inward qualities are good). The ninth woman said: My husband is one with a high palace, long sandals (i.e., tall), and much ash (i.e., he is generous). His kitchen is always warm, so there is a lot of ash; his house is a place where people gather for consultation (like a camp, etc.) (i.e., he is a leader and a man of opinion). The tenth woman said: My husband’s name is Malik. And what a fine Malik he is! Malik is even better than my praise. He has many camel enclosures and few pastures (i.e., many camels are slaughtered for hospitality at his place, so they go out to graze less). When the camels hear the sound of music, they are sure they will be slaughtered (it was customary to play music at feasts, so hearing the music, the camels would be sure of being slaughtered). The eleventh woman said: My husband’s name is Abu Zar’—so wow, how excellent is Abu Zar’! He adorned both my ears with jewelry and filled both my arms with fat (i.e., he made me plump and made me very happy), so my soul was at great ease. He found me among sheep and goat herders living at the edge of a mountain, and he made me the owner of horses, camels, fields, and heaps of grain (i.e., I was very lowly and needy, and he made me honorable and wealthy). When I speak, he does not rebuke me. When I sleep, I sleep till late (i.e., I do not have to do any work), and when I drink, I am satisfied. And Abu Zar’s mother—so how excellent is Abu Zar’s mother! She has large bundles and a spacious house. Abu Zar’s son—so how excellent is Abu Zar’s son! His sleeping place is like the sheath of a sword (i.e., he has a delicate body), and the hand of a (goat) halwan satisfies him (i.e., he eats little). Abu Zar’s daughter—so how excellent is Abu Zar’s daughter! Obedient to her parents and fills out her clothes (i.e., she is plump), and is the envy of her co-wife (i.e., she is beloved to her husband, so her co-wife is jealous of her). And Abu Zar’s slave-girl—so how excellent is Abu Zar’s slave-girl! She does not reveal our secrets, does not take away our food, and does not leave our house dirty with trash. Abu Zar’ went out while milk was being churned in the waterskins. He met a woman who had two sons with her, like two cheetahs, playing with two pomegranates in her lap. So Abu Zar’ divorced me and married that woman. Then I married after him a noble man, who is a fine horseman and spear-bearer. He gave me many livestock and paired every animal for me, and he said to me: O Umm Zar’! Eat yourself and feed your people as well. But if I gather all that my second husband gave me, it would not equal even the smallest vessel of Abu Zar’ (i.e., the favor of the second husband is far less than that of the first). Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: I am to you as Abu Zar’ was to Umm Zar’, (but I have neither divorced you nor will I do so)."
"1670","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja’far says that I heard Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) in Kufa, he was saying that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Among all the women in the heavens and the earth, Maryam bint ‘Imran is the most virtuous, and among all the women in the heavens and the earth, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid (may Allah be pleased with her) is the most virtuous. Abu Kurayb said that Waki’ pointed towards the heavens and the earth."
"1671","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! This is Khadijah coming to you with a vessel in which there is curry, or food, or drink. When she comes to you, convey to her greetings of peace from her Lord and from me, and give her the glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearls, in which there will be neither noise nor any hardship."
"1672","‘Umm al-Mu’minin A’ishah Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I did not feel jealous of any of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her), although I did not see her. Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered a goat, he would say: “Send its meat to Khadijah’s friends.” One day I made you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angry and said: “Khadijah?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Her love has been placed in my heart.”"
"1673","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not marry another woman over Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) until she passed away."
"1674","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Khadijah's (may Allah be pleased with her) sister, Halah bint Khuwaylid, sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he remembered the way Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) used to seek permission. He became happy and said, ""O Allah! Halah bint Khuwaylid."" I felt jealous, so I said, ""Do you remember one of the old women of Quraysh, one with red gums (i.e., extremely old, with no teeth left, only redness), who died long ago, while Allah has given you someone better than her (a young virgin like me)?"""
"1675","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said (to his wives): “The one among you who will meet me first (after death) is the one whose hand is the longest.” So all the noble wives measured their hands to find out whose hand was the longest. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that among all of us, the hands of Sayyida Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) were the longest, because she used to work with her hands and give charity."
"1676","Abu Uthman narrates from Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: If you can, do not be the first to enter the market, nor the last to leave it, because the market is the battlefield of Satan and it is there that he plants his flag. He said: I was informed that Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) was with him. Jibreel (peace be upon him) began talking to him, then stood up (i.e., left). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked her: Who was this man? She said: That was Dihyah Kalbi. Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: By Allah, we thought it was Dihyah Kalbi, until I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) giving a sermon, in which he informed us about it. I (the narrator of the hadith) said: I asked Abu Uthman, from whom did you hear this hadith? He replied: From Sayyiduna Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1677","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would not enter the house of any woman except his wives or Umm Sulaym (who was the mother of Sayyiduna Anas and the wife of Sayyiduna Abu Talhah, may Allah be pleased with them). The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to visit Umm Sulaym. People asked about the reason for this, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I have great compassion for her; her brother was killed while fighting alongside me."""
"1678","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: I entered Paradise, and there I heard the sound of footsteps. So I asked, ""Who is it?"" The people said, ""Ghumaisa bint Milhan (the name of Umm Sulaym was Ghumaisa or Rumaisa), the mother of Anas bin Malik."""
"1679","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that´ Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) after the passing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Come with us to visit Umm Ayman, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to visit her."" When we reached her, she began to weep. Both companions said to her, ""Why are you weeping? Whatever is with Allah, the Majestic and Glorious, for His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) is better for him."" Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""I do not weep because I am unaware of this, but I weep because the revelation from the sky has now ceased."" Upon her saying this, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) also began to weep, and so they wept along with her."
"1680","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: We used to call Zaid bin Harithah as Zaid bin Muhammad (because the Prophet ﷺ had called him his adopted son), until it was revealed in the Qur'an: ""Call them by (the names of) their fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allah."" (Al-Ahzab: 5)."
"1681","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, while he was on the pulpit: ""If you find fault with his leadership (by this he meant Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with him), then indeed you had also found fault with his father's (Zaid's) leadership before this. By Allah! His father was worthy of leadership and was the dearest of all people to me. And by Allah! He (i.e., Usama) is also worthy of leadership, and by Allah! After him, Usama is the dearest of all people to me. Therefore, I advise you to treat Usama well, for he is one of the blessed among you."""
"1682","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Bilal after the morning prayer: ""O Bilal! Tell me about the deed you have done in Islam for which you have the greatest hope of reward, for I heard the sound of your footsteps ahead of me in Paradise last night."" Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""I have not done any deed in Islam for which I have greater hope of benefit except that whenever I perform ablution, whether by night or by day, I pray as much as Allah has destined for me with that ablution."""
"1683","Narrated from Sayyiduna ‘Aidh bin ‘Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Salman, Suhaib, and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them) were sitting among some other people when Sayyiduna Abu Sufyan came to them. They said, “The swords of Allah did not strike the neck of Allah’s enemy at their proper time (i.e., this enemy of Allah was not killed).” Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Do you say such things about the elder and chief of Quraysh?” (Sayyiduna Abu Bakr said this out of consideration, lest Abu Sufyan become displeased and not accept Islam.) Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “O Abu Bakr! Perhaps you have angered those people (i.e., Salman, Suhaib, and Bilal, may Allah be pleased with them)? If you have angered them, then you have angered your Lord.” Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) went to those people and said, “O my brothers! Did I anger you?” They replied, “O our brother! No, may Allah forgive you.”"
"1684","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` my mother brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and had torn her shawl or scarf into two parts, making a lower garment for me from one half and an upper garment from the other half. She said, ""O Messenger of Allah! This Anas is my little son; I have brought him to you to serve you. Please pray for him."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Increase him in wealth and children."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says, ""My wealth is abundant and today my sons and grandsons are more than a hundred."" (__QUR_N__, __XREF_N__, __REF_N__)"
"1685","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was passing by when my mother, Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her), heard your (peace and blessings be upon him) voice and said, ""May my parents be sacrificed for you (peace and blessings be upon him), this is little Anas."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made three supplications for me. Two of them I have received in this world, and I hope for the third in the Hereafter."
"1686","Thabit narrates from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I was playing with (my peers) children when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me, he greeted us with salam and sent me for some task. I went late to my mother, so my mother asked, ""Why were you late?"" I said, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me for a task."" She said, ""What was the task?"" I said, ""It is a secret."" My mother said, ""Do not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to anyone."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""By Allah, if I were to tell that secret to anyone, O Thabit! I would have told you."""
"1687","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were in Yemen when news reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had left Makkah. So we also set out to migrate towards him (peace be upon him). I and my two brothers—one was Abu Burdah and the other Abu Ruhm—I was the youngest of them, and fifty-three or fifty-two, or he said, a little over fifty men from my people came with us. Sayyiduna Abu Musa says: We all boarded a ship. By coincidence, this ship took us to the land of Abyssinia, to the king Najashi. There we met Sayyiduna Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) ibn Abi Talib and his companions. Sayyiduna Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has sent us here and ordered us to stay here, so you also stay with us. So we stayed with them. Then we all set out together and reached the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when he had already conquered Khaybar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) allotted us a share from the spoils of that place, and no one who was absent from the battle of Khaybar received a share except for the people of our ship. And some people began to say to us (i.e., the people of the ship) that in migration, we have preceded you. And Sayyidah Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her), who had come with us, went to meet Umm al-Mu'mineen Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her), and she too had migrated with the emigrants to the land of Najashi. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Umm al-Mu'mineen Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) while Sayyidah Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her) was present with her. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) and asked: Who is this? Umm al-Mu'mineen Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: This is Asma bint Umais. So he said: The one who went to the land of Abyssinia and has now come by sea? Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: Yes, I am she. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We have preceded you in migration, therefore we have more right to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) than you. Hearing this, she became angry and said: ""O Umar! By Allah, never! You have lied. You were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), among you the hungry were fed and your ignorant were advised, and we were in a distant land, the land of enemies, Abyssinia, and all our hardships were in the way of Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him). By Allah! Food and drink are forbidden to me until I mention your words to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). We were harmed and were always in fear. Soon I will mention this to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), I will ask him, and by Allah, I will neither lie nor deviate nor say more than this."" When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived, Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) has said such and such. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No one has more right than you. For Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and his companions have one migration, and you, the people of the ship, have two migrations (one from Makkah to Abyssinia and the other from Abyssinia to Madinah Tayyibah). Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I saw Abu Musa and the people of the ship coming to me in groups and listening to this hadith. And there was nothing in the world more pleasing or greater to them than this statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Sayyiduna Abu Burdah said that Sayyidah Asma said: I saw Abu Musa wanting to hear this hadith from me again and again (out of happiness)."
"1688","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would return from a journey, he would meet the people. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja'far says that once he met me and Hasan or Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated one of us in front of him and one behind him, until we came to Madinah."
"1689","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to the toilet (to relieve himself), so I placed water for ablution for him. When he came out, he asked, ""Who placed this water?"" The people or I said, ""Ibn Abbas did."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Grant him understanding of the religion."""
"1690","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that during the blessed life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when anyone saw a dream, he would relate it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). I also wished that I would see a dream and relate it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). I was a young, unmarried boy, and during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I used to sleep in the mosque. I saw in a dream that two angels took hold of me and led me towards Hell. I saw that it was like a deep well, layered upon layers, and over it were two wooden beams like those placed over a well. There were some people in it whom I recognized. I began to say, ""I seek refuge in Allah from Hell, I seek refuge in Allah from Hell,"" three times. Then I met another angel who said, ""You have nothing to fear."" I related this dream to Umm al-Mu'mineen Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her). She then related it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Abdullah is a good man if only he would pray Tahajjud at night."" Salim said that after that, Abdullah would sleep only a little part of the night (and would spend the rest in prayer)."
"1691","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Mulaikah reports that’ Abdullah bin Ja’far (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him): Do you remember when I, you, and Ibn Abbas met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? So Sayyiduna Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Yes, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made us ride (with him) and left you (behind) (because there was not enough space on the mount)."
"1692","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when this verse was revealed: ""Those who believe and do righteous deeds, there is no sin upon them for what they have eaten..."" till the end, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me that it has been said to me that you are among those people (i.e., among the believers and those who do righteous deeds)."
"1693","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: My brother and I came from Yemen, and for a time we considered Abdullah bin Mas'ud and his mother to be among the family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), because they used to visit him frequently and stay with him."
"1694","Abu’l-Ahwas says: We were in the house of Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), and there were several companions of Abdullah ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) there, and they were looking at a copy of the Qur’an, when suddenly Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up. Abu Mas’ud said: I do not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) left behind anyone after him who knew the Qur’an better than the person who has just stood up. Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If you say this (then it is correct), and his condition was such that when we were absent, he was present, and when we were prevented, he was granted permission (to go to the Messenger of Allah)."
"1695","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""And whoever conceals anything, he will bring it forth on the Day of Resurrection."" (Surah: Aal-e-Imran: 161) Then he said: ""To whose recitation do you command me to recite the Qur'an? I have recited more than seventy surahs before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) know that I am most knowledgeable of Allah's Book among them. And if I knew that anyone was more knowledgeable of Allah's Book than me, I would travel to him."" Shafeeq said: ""I have sat in the circles of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I have not heard anyone rejecting the statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) or finding fault with him."""
"1696","Masruq says: We were with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them) when we mentioned Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them). He said: You have mentioned a person whom I have loved ever since I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I heard him say: Learn the Qur'an from four people: from the son of Umm Abd (i.e., Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud)—and he (the Prophet) started with him—and from Ubayy bin Ka'b, and from Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhaifah, and from Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"1697","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: My father was martyred on the day of Uhud, so I would lift the cloth from his face and weep. People would stop me, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would not stop me. And Amr's daughter Fatimah (that is, my paternal aunt) was also weeping over him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whether you weep or not, until you lifted him up, the angels were shading him with their wings."
"1698","Sayyiduna Amir bin Sa’d says: I heard my father (may Allah be pleased with him) say that I did not hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about any living person who walks around that he is in Paradise, except for Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him). (This is his own information, otherwise many companions received the glad tidings of Paradise, such as the ten who were given glad tidings, etc.)"
"1699","Khursha bin Har says: I was sitting in a circle in the mosque of Madinah, and there was also a handsome old man there. It became known that he was Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him). He was speaking good things to the people. When he stood up, the people said, ""Whoever wishes to see a person of Paradise, let him look at him."" I said (in my heart), ""By Allah, I will go with him and see his house."" Then I followed him. He walked until he was about to leave the city, then he went into his house, so I also asked for permission to enter. He gave permission, then asked, ""O my nephew! What do you need?"" I said, ""When you stood up, I heard the people say, 'Whoever wishes to see a person of Paradise, let him look at him,' so I wished to be with you."" He said, ""Allah knows best about the people of Paradise, and I will tell you the reason why people say this about me. Once I was sleeping, and in my dream a person came and said, 'Get up.' Then he took my hand, and I went with him. I found some paths on the left side, so I wanted to go on them, but he said, 'Do not go on them; these are the paths of the people of the left (i.e., the disbelievers).' Then I found some paths on the right side, so that person said, 'Go on these paths.' So he brought me to a mountain and said, 'Climb it.' I tried to climb up, but I fell on my back. Many times I tried to climb, but each time I fell. Then he took me along until we came to a pillar whose top was in the sky and its base in the earth, and on top of it was a ring. That person said to me, 'Climb up this pillar.' I said, 'How can I climb it when its top is in the sky?' Finally, that person took my hand and lifted me up, and I saw that I was hanging, holding onto that ring. Then that person struck the pillar, so it fell, and I remained hanging on that ring until morning (because there was no way to get down)."" He says, ""Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and related my dream to him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'The paths you saw on the left are the paths of the people of the left, and the paths you saw on the right are the paths of the people of the right. And that mountain is the station of the martyrs; you will not reach there. And the pillar is the pillar of Islam, and the ring is the ring of Islam, and you will remain firm upon Islam until you die.' (And when one dies upon Islam, Paradise is certain, and that is why people call me a person of Paradise.)"""
"1700","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, while the funeral of Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) was placed before them, that the Throne of the Lord shook for him."
"1701","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a silk garment was presented as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). His companions began to touch it and were amazed at its softness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Are you amazed at its softness? Indeed, the handkerchiefs of Sa’d bin Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) in Paradise are better and softer than this.”"
"1702","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) had a son from Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) who passed away. She told her family members not to inform Abu Talhah about his son until she herself told him. Eventually, Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) came home, and Sayyidah Umm Sulaym presented the evening meal before him. He ate and drank, then Umm Sulaym adorned herself well for him until he had intercourse with her. When Umm Sulaym saw that he was satisfied and had been intimate with her, she said, “O Abu Talhah! If some people entrust something to the people of a household and then ask for it back, can the household prevent them from taking it?” Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, “No, they cannot prevent them.” Sayyidah Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “Then hope for reward from Allah for your son (because the son had passed away).” Upon hearing this, Abu Talhah became angry and said, “You kept me unaware until I became impure with you (i.e., had intercourse), and now you inform me about my son?” He went and informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about this. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “May Allah bless you in the night you have spent.” Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) became pregnant. It is narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey, and Umm Sulaym was with him. Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returned from a journey to Madinah, he would not enter Madinah at night. When the people neared Madinah, Umm Sulaym began experiencing labor pains, and Abu Talhah stayed with her while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) proceeded. Abu Talhah said, “O Lord! You know that I love to go out with Your Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) when he goes out, and to enter with him when he enters, but You know the reason I have stayed behind.” Umm Sulaym said, “O Abu Talhah! I no longer feel the pain as before, so let us go.” So we set out, and when both of us reached Madinah, Umm Sulaym again began experiencing labor pains and gave birth to a boy. My mother said, “O Anas! Do not let anyone nurse him until you take him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the morning.” When morning came, I took the child and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When I arrived, I saw that he had an iron tool for branding camels in his hand. When he saw me, he said, “Perhaps Umm Sulaym has given birth to a boy?” I said, “Yes.” He put the tool down from his blessed hand, and I placed the child in his lap. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called for some dates of Madinah (ajwah), chewed them in his blessed mouth, and when they became soft, he put them into the child’s mouth. The child began to suck on them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “See how much the Ansar love dates!” Then he passed his hand over the child’s face and named him Abdullah."
"1703","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), four persons compiled the Qur'an, and all four were Ansari. Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal, Ubayy bin Ka'b, Zayd bin Thabit, and Abu Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them). Qatadah said: I asked Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Who is Abu Zayd?"" He said: He was one of my uncles."
"1704","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Samit narrates that’ Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I, my brother Anis, and our mother, all three of us, left our tribe Ghifar, who used to consider even the sacred months as permissible. So we went to stay with one of our maternal uncles. He treated us well and did good to us, but his people became jealous of us and said to him, “When you leave your house, Anis commits adultery with your wife.” He came to us and foolishly spread this rumor. I said, “The favor you did to us has now been spoiled; we can no longer stay with you.” So we went to our camels, loaded our belongings, and our uncle wrapped himself in his cloth and began to weep. We left until we camped in front of Makkah. Anis made a bet with our camels for an equal number of others. Then both went to a soothsayer, and the soothsayer said to Anis, “He is better.” So Anis brought us all the camels and as many more. Abu Dharr said, “O son of my brother! I had performed prayer three years before meeting the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” I asked, “For whom did you pray?” Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “For Allah, the Exalted.” I asked, “In which direction did you face?” He said, “I faced wherever Allah turned my face.” I would pray ‘Isha at the end of the night and would lie like a blanket until the sun rose. Anis said, “I have some work in Makkah; you stay here, I will go.” He went and was delayed in returning. When he came back, I asked, “What did you do?” He replied, “I met a man in Makkah who is upon your religion and says that Allah has sent him.” I asked, “What do people call him?” He said, “People call him a poet, a soothsayer, and a magician.” Anis himself was a poet. He said, “I have heard the words of soothsayers, but the words this man recites are not those of soothsayers. I have measured his speech against all the meters of poetry, but after me, it will not fit anyone’s tongue like poetry. By Allah, he is truthful and the people are liars.” I said, “You stay here, I will go and see this man.” Then I came to Makkah and picked out a weak person from among the people of Makkah (because a strong person might harm me), and asked him, “Where is the man whom you call a Sabi’ (renegade)?” He pointed at me and said, “This is the Sabi’ (since you are asking about the Sabi’).” Hearing this, all the people of the valley attacked me with stones and bones until I fell unconscious. When I regained consciousness and stood up, I saw myself as if I were a red idol (i.e., covered in blood from head to toe). Then I came to Zamzam, washed off all the blood, and drank Zamzam water. So, O my nephew! I stayed there for thirty nights or thirty days, and I had no food except Zamzam water (whenever I felt hungry, I drank it). Then I became fat until the folds of my belly hung down (from obesity), and I did not feel any weakness from hunger in my chest. Once, the people of Makkah slept on a moonlit night, and at that time no one was performing Tawaf of the Ka’bah except two women who were calling upon Isaf and Na’ila (Isaf and Na’ila were two idols in Makkah; Isaf was a man and Na’ila was a woman, and the disbelievers believed that both had committed adultery there, so they were transformed into idols). They came before me while performing Tawaf. I said, “Marry one to the other (i.e., Isaf to Na’ila).” Even after hearing this, they did not desist from their act. Then I openly said, “Put a stick in their private parts (i.e., this obscenity is due to the worship of Isaf and Na’ila),” and I did not use a euphemism (i.e., I did not use indirect language but openly cursed Isaf and Na’ila to anger those accursed women who, in the House of Allah, called upon Isaf and Na’ila instead of Allah). Hearing this, both women screamed and left, saying, “If only there were someone from our people here (who would punish this man for his disrespect)!” On the way, they met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), who were descending from the mountain. They asked the women, “What happened?” They replied, “A Sabi’ has come who is hiding in the curtains of the Ka’bah.” They asked, “What did this Sabi’ say?” They replied, “He said something that fills the mouth (i.e., we cannot utter it).” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came, kissed the Black Stone, performed Tawaf with his companion, and prayed. When they finished the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I was the first to offer the greeting and said, ‘Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah!’” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah.” Then he asked, “Who are you?” I said, “A man from Ghifar.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) lowered his hand and placed his fingers on his forehead (as if in remembrance). I thought to myself, perhaps he disliked that I said I was from (the tribe of) Ghifar. I reached out to take the Prophet’s hand, but his companion (Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him), who knew more about the Prophet’s condition than I did, stopped me. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head and asked, “When did you come here?” I replied, “I have been here for thirty nights or days.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “Who feeds you?” I said, “Nothing except Zamzam water.” Then I became fat until the folds of my belly bent, and I do not feel any weakness from hunger in my chest. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Zamzam water is blessed; it is food and fills the belly like food.” Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to feed him tonight.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) left, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and I went with them. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) opened a door and brought out some dried grapes from Ta’if; this was the first food I ate in Makkah. Then I stayed as long as I stayed, and after that I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said, “A land of date palms has been shown to me; I think that land is none other than Yathrib.” (Yathrib was the name of Madinah.) “So, on my behalf, invite your people to the religion; perhaps Allah will benefit them through you and reward you.” I went to Anis, and he asked, “What did you do?” I said, “I have accepted Islam and affirmed the Prophethood of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” He said, “I do not dislike your religion; I too have accepted Islam and affirmed his Prophethood.” Then we both went to our mother, and she said, “I do not dislike your religion either; I too have accepted Islam and affirmed it.” Then we loaded our belongings on the camels until we reached our tribe Ghifar. Half of the tribe became Muslim, and their leader was Ima’ bin Rahda Ghifari, who was also their chief. The other half said, “When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) comes to Madinah, we will become Muslim.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Madinah, and the remaining half also became Muslim. The people of (the tribe of) Aslam came and said, “O Messenger of Allah! We too become Muslim like our Ghifari brothers.” So they also became Muslim. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Allah has forgiven Ghifar, and Allah has saved Aslam (from killing and captivity).”"
"1705","‘Abdullah bin ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that when Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) heard the news of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being sent in Makkah, he said to his brother, “Mount your ride and go to this valley and see that person who claims that news comes to him from the sky. Listen to what he says and then come back to me.” So his brother set out, until he reached Makkah and heard the words of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then returned to Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, “I have seen that person; he commands good character and recites a speech which is not poetry.” Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “This did not satisfy me.” Then he himself took provisions and a water-skin until he reached Makkah and entered Masjid al-Haram. There he searched for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but did not recognize him, nor did he consider it appropriate to ask. Night fell and he lay down. ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) saw him and recognized that he was a traveler, so he followed him, but neither spoke to the other until morning came. Then he brought his provisions and water-skin to the mosque and stayed there all day, but did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until evening. Then he went to his sleeping place. ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by and said, “Has the time not come for this man to know his place?” Then he stood him up and took him along, but neither spoke to the other. The same happened on the third day. ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stood him up and took him along, then said, “Why do you not tell me the reason for which you have come to this city?” Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “If you promise and pledge to guide me, I will tell you.” ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) promised, so he told him. ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “That person is truthful and he is indeed the Messenger of Allah. In the morning, walk with me. If I see anything that makes me fear for your life, I will stand as if pouring water (i.e., I will pretend to urinate), and if I move on, then follow me. Wherever I enter, you also enter.” Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) did so and followed him until ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) also reached with him. Then Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) listened to the words of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam right there. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Go to your people and inform them about the religion until my command reaches you.” Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I will proclaim this (i.e., my acceptance of Islam) to the people of Makkah.” Then Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) came out to the mosque and proclaimed loudly, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the true Messenger of Allah.” The people attacked him and beat him until he fell down. ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) came and leaned over Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said to the people, “Woe to you! Do you not know that this man is from (the tribe of) Ghifar, and your trade route to Syria passes through the land of Ghifar (so they may cut off your trade)?” Then he rescued Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) from them. The next day, Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) did the same, and the people rushed and beat him, and ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) came and rescued him."
"1706","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was at that time at Ji'ranah, between Makkah and Madinah, and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was with him. Then a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you not fulfill your promise to me?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Rejoice."" He replied, ""You say 'rejoice' a lot."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned in anger towards Sayyiduna Abu Musa and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said, ""He has rejected the glad tidings, but you both accept it."" Both said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We have accepted."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for a bowl of water, washed his hands and face in it, put some of his saliva in it, and said to both of them, ""Drink from this water, pour it over your faces and chests, and rejoice."" Both of them took the bowl and did so. Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) called out to them from behind a curtain, ""Leave some water in the vessel for your mother as well."" So both of them left some water in the vessel for her."
"1707","‘Sayyiduna Abu Burdah narrates from his father Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the battle of Hunayn, he sent Sayyiduna Abu Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) with an army to Autas, where he confronted Duraid bin as-Simmah. Duraid bin as-Simmah was killed, and Allah granted defeat to those with him. Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had also sent me with Sayyiduna Abu Amir (may Allah be pleased with him). Then, an arrow from a man of Banu Jusham struck Sayyiduna Abu Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) in the knee and became lodged in his knee. I went to him and asked, “O uncle! Who shot you with this arrow?” He said, “This man killed me, and this man shot me with the arrow.” Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I pursued that man and caught up with him. When he saw me, he turned his back and fled. I chased after him and began to say, ‘O shameless one! Are you not an Arab? Will you not stand your ground?’ So he stopped. Then I confronted him; he struck at me and I struck at him, and finally, I killed him with my sword. Then I returned to Abu Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ‘Allah has caused the killer to be killed.’ Abu Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ‘Now pull out this arrow.’ I pulled it out, and water came out from the place of the arrow (not blood; perhaps the arrow was poisoned). Abu Amir said, ‘O my nephew! Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and convey my greetings, and say: Pray for Abu Amir’s forgiveness.’ Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ‘Abu Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) made me the leader of the people, and he lived for a short while, then passed away.’ When I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he was in a small room on a bed made of palm fibers, which had left marks on his back and sides. I said, ‘Abu Amir requested you to pray for his forgiveness.’ So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called for water, performed ablution, then raised both hands and said, ‘O Allah! Forgive Ubaid Abu Amir (his name was Ubaid bin Sulaim),’ until I saw the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then he said, ‘O Allah! Make Abu Amir the leader of many people on the Day of Resurrection.’ I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah! Pray for my forgiveness as well.’ So he said, ‘O Allah! Forgive the sins of Abdullah bin Qais and grant him an honorable place on the Day of Resurrection.’ Abu Burdah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ‘One supplication was made for Abu Amir and one supplication was made for Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with them both).’"
"1708","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I used to invite my mother to Islam and she was a polytheist. One day I asked her to accept Islam, but she said something about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I disliked. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping and said, ""I used to invite my mother to Islam but she would not accept. Today she said something about you that I disliked, so please supplicate to Allah that He may guide the mother of Abu Hurairah."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Guide the mother of Abu Hurairah."" I left, happy with the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When I reached home and arrived at the door, it was closed. My mother heard the sound of my footsteps and said, ""Wait a moment."" I heard the sound of water falling; in short, my mother performed ghusl, put on her shirt, quickly covered herself, then opened the door and said, ""O Abu Hurairah! I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the servant and Messenger of Allah."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping with joy and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Rejoice, Allah has accepted your supplication and guided the mother of Abu Hurairah."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised Allah, mentioned His attributes, and spoke good words. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, that He may place love for me and my mother in the hearts of the Muslims, and their love in our hearts."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Place the love of Your servants, that is, Abu Hurairah and his mother, in the hearts of the believing servants, and place the love of the believers in their hearts."" After that, no believer was born who heard me or saw me except that he loved me."
"1709","‘Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “Are you not amazed at Abu Hurairah? He came and sat in one corner of my room and began narrating hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I was listening, but I was performing voluntary prayers, and he left before I finished. If I had found him, I would have refuted him, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not speak in such haste as you do.” Ibn Shihab said to Ibn al-Musayyib: “Indeed, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ‘People say that Abu Hurairah narrates many hadith, and Allah is the examiner, and they also say: Why do the Muhajirun and Ansar not narrate hadith as Abu Hurairah does? Soon I will explain the reason to you. My Ansari brothers were busy working in their fields, and the Muhajirun were occupied with business in the markets, but I would stay with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to fill my stomach. Thus, I would be present while they were absent, and I would remember while they would forget. One day, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Who among you will spread out his garment and listen to my hadith, then gather it to his chest, so that he will not forget anything he hears?” I spread out my cloak until he finished speaking, then I gathered it to my chest. From that day, I have not forgotten anything that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said. And if it were not for these two verses that were revealed in the Noble Qur’an, I would not narrate any hadith to anyone: ‘Indeed, those who conceal what We have sent down of clear proofs and guidance…’ to the end.” __QUR_N__ __XREF_N__ __REF_N__"
"1710","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) held a sword on the day of Uhud and said, ""Who will take this from me?"" People stretched out their hands and each one was saying, ""I will take it, I will take it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Who will fulfill its right?"" Upon hearing this, people withdrew (because on the day of Uhud the disbelievers had the upper hand). Sayyiduna Simak bin Kharsha Abu Dujana (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I will fulfill its right."" Then he took it and split the heads of the polytheists with that sword."
"1711","Abu Zumail says that Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to me and said: The Muslims did not pay attention to Abu Sufyan, nor did they sit with him (because Abu Sufyan had fought against the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, several times and was a fierce enemy of the Muslims). Once, he spoke to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant me three things. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Very well. Abu Sufyan said: I have a woman who is the most beautiful and attractive among all the Arabs, Umm Habibah, my daughter; I will marry her to you. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Very well. The second (request) is that make my son Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) your scribe. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Very well. The third is, command me to fight against the disbelievers (just as before Islam I used to fight against the Muslims). The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Very well. Abu Zumail said: If he had not asked for these things from the Prophet, peace be upon him, the Prophet would not have given them, because (it was the habit of the Prophet, peace be upon him) that whenever anyone asked him for something, he would agree."
"1712","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a military expedition, and Allah Almighty granted him (victory along with) spoils of war. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to his people, ""Is there anyone absent among you?"" The people replied, ""Yes, so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so are absent."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""Is there anyone else absent?"" The people said, ""So-and-so and so-and-so are absent."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Is there anyone else absent?"" The people replied, ""No one."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""I do not see Julaibib (may Allah be pleased with him)."" The people searched for him among the dead and found his body near seven corpses whom Sayyiduna Julaibib had killed. He killed seven and was then martyred. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came to him, stood there, and then said, ""He killed seven men, and then he was killed. He is of me and I am of him."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) lifted him with his own two hands, and only the Prophet's hands served as his bier. After that, a grave was dug and he was placed in it. And the narrator did not mention the washing (ghusl)."
"1713","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by Sayyiduna Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was reciting poetry in the mosque. (It is understood that reciting poetry in the mosque which praises Islam, criticizes disbelievers, or encourages jihad is permissible.) Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) looked at him (angrily). Sayyiduna Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I used to recite poetry in the mosque even when a person better than you (i.e., the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him) was present."" Then he looked towards Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""I ask you by Allah, did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? He used to say: 'O Hassan! Reply on my behalf. O Allah, help him with the Holy Spirit (Jibreel, peace be upon him).'"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Yes, I heard it. O Allah, You know."""
"1714","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he used to say to Sayyiduna Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him): Satirize (the disbelievers), and Jibreel is with you. (To mention someone’s faults is called satire.)"
"1715","Masruq says: I went to Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), and with her was Sayyiduna Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), who was reciting a verse from his ghazal, which was a few couplets he had composed. The verse was: ""Pure and intelligent, there is no accusation against them. They rise in the morning hungry for the flesh of the heedless."" (Meaning, they do not backbite anyone, because backbiting is as if eating their flesh.) Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said to Sayyiduna Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him): ""But you are not like that"" (meaning, you do backbite people). Masruq said: I asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): ""Why do you allow Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him) to come to you, even though Allah Almighty has said about him: 'The person among them who took upon himself the greater part of it (i.e., the slander against Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her)), for him is a great punishment.'"" (Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) was among those who participated in the slander against Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prescribed the legal punishment for him.) Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""What greater punishment could there be than that he became blind?"" And she said: ""He used to defend or satirize on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) against the disbelievers."" (That is why I allow him to come to me.)"
"1716","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Satirize the Quraysh, for satire is more distressing to them than a shower of arrows. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a person to Sayyiduna Ibn Rawaha (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: Satirize the Quraysh. He composed satire, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not like it. Then he sent to Sayyiduna Ka’b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him). Then he sent to Sayyiduna Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). When Sayyiduna Hassan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: The time has come upon you that you have called this lion who strikes with his tail (meaning, he kills people with his tongue, as if he is a lion in the field of eloquence and poetry). Then he stuck out his tongue and began to move it and said: By Him Who sent you as a true Prophet, I will tear the disbelievers apart with my tongue as leather is torn apart. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Hassan! Do not be hasty! For Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) knows the genealogy of the Quraysh very well, and my lineage is also from the Quraysh, so he will separate my lineage for you. Then Hassan went to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), then returned and said: O Messenger of Allah! Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) has explained your lineage to me. By Him Who sent you as a true Prophet, I will extract you from among the Quraysh as a hair is taken out from flour. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say to Hassan: The Holy Spirit will always help you as long as you answer on behalf of Allah and His Messenger. And Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: When Hassan satirized the Quraysh, he healed the hearts of the believers and destroyed the honor of the disbelievers. Hassan said: You reviled Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so I replied to you, and Allah will recompense for that. You reviled Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), who is righteous and pious, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and loyalty is his trait. My forefathers and my honor are sacrificed to protect the honor of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). If you do not see dust rising from both sides of Kada’ (the pass at the gate of Mecca), then I would lose my life. Such she-camels that will pull hard on the reins and climb up with their strength and power, on their shoulders are those spears which are thin or thirsty for blood, and our horses will come running, their mouths wiped by women with their veils. If you do not speak to us, we will perform Umrah, and victory will be achieved, and the veil will be lifted. Otherwise, be patient for the blow of that day when Allah will honor whom He wills. And Allah has said: I have prepared an army, which is the army of the Ansar, whose sport is to confront the disbelievers. And Allah has said: I have sent a servant who speaks the truth, there is no doubt in his word. Every day we are in one preparation or another, either abuse from the disbelievers, or fighting, or satire against the disbelievers. Whoever among you reviles the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), or praises him, or helps him, all are equal. Jibreel is among us, the Messenger of Allah, and the Holy Spirit, for whom there is no equal."
"1717","`Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` since I became Muslim, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) never prevented me from entering, and whenever he saw me, he always had a smile on his face (that is, he would meet with cheerfulness and an open forehead)."
"1718","`Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah said to me, ""O Jarir! Will you not relieve me from Dhu al-Khalasah?"" And Dhu al-Khalasah was an idol house of the tribe of Khath'am, which was also called the Yemeni Ka'bah. Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I went there with one hundred and fifty horsemen, and I could not sit firmly on a horse, so I mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He struck his hand on my chest and said, 'O Allah, make him firm and make him one who guides and is guided.' Then Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) went and set Dhu al-Khalasah on fire. After that, a man named Abu Artat was sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to give the good news. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, 'We have left Dhu al-Khalasah like a mangy camel.' (A mangy camel is smeared with black oil, meaning it too had become blackened by burning.) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for blessings five times for the horses and men of the tribe of Ahmas."
"1719","Narrated from Sayyida Umm Mubashshir (may Allah be pleased with her) that she heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying to Umm al-Mu’minin Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) that, if Allah wills, none of the people of the Tree will enter Hell. That is, those who pledged allegiance under the tree. She said, “O Messenger of Allah! Why will they not enter?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) rebuked her. Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that Allah Almighty says: “There is not one of you but will pass over it (Hell)” (Surah Maryam: 71). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah Almighty says: “Then We will save those who feared Allah and leave the wrongdoers within it, on their knees” (Surah Maryam: 72)."
"1720","‘Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me, Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) to the place of Rawdat Khakh and said: Go, and there you will find a woman riding a camel. She has a letter with her; take it from her and bring it back. We set off quickly on our horses, and suddenly we found the woman. We said to her: Hand over the letter. She said: I do not have any letter. We said: Produce the letter, or else remove your clothes. So she took out the letter from her garments. We brought that letter to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). It was written from Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah to some of the polytheists of Makkah, and it mentioned some matters of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). (In one narration, it is mentioned that Hatib informed the disbelievers about the preparations and readiness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and the departure to Makkah.) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Hatib! What is this that you have done? He said: O Messenger of Allah! Do not be hasty (i.e., do not punish me immediately; please listen to my situation). I was a person attached to the Quraysh, meaning I was their ally, but not one of them. The Muhajirun who are with you have relatives among the Quraysh, because of whom their households are protected. So I wanted, since I have no ties with the Quraysh, to do something for them so that they would protect my family and dependents. I did not do this out of disbelief or apostasy, nor did I do it after becoming Muslim out of pleasure with disbelief. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Hatib has spoken the truth. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to strike the neck of this hypocrite. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He participated in the Battle of Badr, and you do not know that Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish (so long as it does not reach disbelief), I have forgiven you. Then Allah revealed this verse: “O you who believe! Do not take My enemies and your enemies as friends...” (Surah Al-Mumtahanah: 1)."
"1721","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Quraysh, Ansar, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Aslam, Ghifar, and Ashja‘ (all these tribes) are friends, and besides Allah and His Messenger, they have no protector."""
"1722","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that the women of Quraysh are the best women who have ever ridden camels; they are the most compassionate to their children (when they are young) and the best guardians of their husbands’ wealth. (The narrator says that) Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say that Sayyidah Maryam bint ‘Imran (may Allah be pleased with her) never rode a camel."
"1723","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that this verse: ""When two parties among you were about to lose heart, but Allah was their protector"" (Aal-e-Imran: 122) was revealed about us, meaning Banu Salamah and Banu Harithah. And we do not wish that this verse had not been revealed, because Allah Almighty says: ""And Allah was their protector."""
"1724","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah! Forgive the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the grandsons of the Ansar (also forgive them)."
"1725","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw children and women coming from a wedding, so he (peace be upon him) stood in front of them and said: O people! You are the most beloved to me among all people. O people! You are the most beloved to me among all people. That is, he said this to the people of the Ansar."
"1726","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for forgiveness for the Ansar, for the children of the Ansar, and for the slaves of the Ansar."
"1727","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Ansar are my intestines and my bundles (meaning, those who keep my clothes, i.e., my special trusted and reliable people). And people will increase while the Ansar will decrease, so accept their good deeds and overlook their faults."""
"1728","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Usaid Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best house among the Ansar is that of Banu Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu Harith bin Khazraj, then Banu Sa‘idah, and there is goodness in every house of the Ansar. Abu Salamah said that Sayyiduna Abu Usaid said: Do you think I would accuse the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? If I were lying, I would have mentioned my own tribe, Banu Sa‘idah, first. When this news reached Sayyiduna Sa‘d bin ‘Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him), he was grieved and began to say: We have been left behind, we are the last of the four. Saddle my donkey so that I may go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The nephew of Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: Are you going to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to refute his words, even though he knows best? Is it not enough for you that you are the fourth among the four? Hearing this, Sayyiduna Sa‘d turned back and said: Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) know best, and he ordered the saddle to be removed from the donkey."
"1729","‘Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I went out on a journey with Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah Bajali (may Allah be pleased with him), and he used to serve me. I said to him, “Do not serve me (because you are older).” He said, “I have seen the Ansar doing work with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so I have sworn that whenever I am with any of the Ansar, I will serve him (i.e., the way the Ansar treated you and protected you from the enemy, etc.).” And Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) was older than Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1730","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I recognize the voices of the Ash‘aris from their recitation of the Qur’an when they come at night, and I also recognize their dwellings by their voices at night, even though I have not seen their dwellings during the day when they descend during the day. And among them is a wise man who, when he meets the cavalry of the disbelievers or the enemy, says to them: “Our people say to you, give us some respite or wait a little,” meaning, “We too are ready and coming to fight.” (That is, he saves himself with wisdom and prudence, because the enemy thinks that he is not alone, but that there are others with him.)"
"1731","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Indeed, when the people of the Ash‘ari tribe run short of provisions during a battle, or when the food of their families in Madinah becomes scarce, they gather whatever they have in a cloth and then distribute it equally among themselves. These people are from me and I am from them (meaning I am pleased with them and I like such unity)."
"1732","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has kept (the tribe of) Aslam safe and has forgiven (the tribe of) Ghifar, and this is not what I say, rather Allah the Exalted says it."
"1733","‘Sayyiduna Khafaf bin Ima’ Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said in his prayer: O Allah! Curse Banu Lihyan, and Ra’l, Dhakwaan, and ‘Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. And Allah forgave (the tribe of) Ghifar and protected (the tribe of) Aslam."
"1734","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that Aqra’ bin Habis (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The people of the tribes Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and Juhaynah, who used to raid the pilgrims, have pledged allegiance. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If (the tribes of) Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and Juhaynah are better than Banu Tamim, Banu Amir, Asad, and Ghatafan, then these people (i.e., Banu Tamim and others) are at a loss and have failed? He said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose hand is my soul, they are better than them (i.e., the tribes of Aslam and Ghifar, etc., are better than the tribe of Banu Tamim and others)."
"1735","Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I came to Sayyiduna ‘Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said to me: The very first charity that brightened the faces of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions (meaning, made them happy) was the charity of the (tribe of) Tayy. (And he said:) That charity was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by you (meaning, ‘Adi bin Hatim)."
"1736","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that Tufail (may Allah be pleased with him) and his companions came and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! (The tribe of) Daws has chosen disbelief and refused to accept Islam, so pray against Daws."" It was said that the people of Daws are destroyed. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Guide Daws and bring them to me."""
"1737","Abu Zar’ah says that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I always love the (tribe of) Banu Tamim for three reasons which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I heard him say that they will be the most severe against the Dajjal among my Ummah. And when their charity came, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: These are the charities of our people. And a woman from this tribe was a captive with Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Set her free, for she is from the descendants of Sayyiduna Isma’il (peace be upon him)."
"1738","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) established brotherhood between Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah al-Jarrah and Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1739","‘Asim Ahwal says that it was said to Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): “Have you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that there is no alliance (hilf) in Islam?” So Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made an alliance between the Quraysh and the Ansar in his house.”"
"1740","Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam (i.e., such an alliance in which there is partnership even in inheritance, etc.), and any oath that was taken in the time of ignorance (for a good cause) has become even stronger with Islam."
"1741","‘Sayyiduna Abu Burdah narrates from his father (may Allah be pleased with him),’ he said: We offered the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then we said that if we remain seated until we also offer the ‘Isha prayer with you, it would be better. So we remained seated, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came out. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Have you been sitting here all this time? We replied: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! We offered the Maghrib prayer with you, then we said that if we remain seated until we also offer the ‘Isha prayer with you, it would be better. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have done well, or you have done right. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head towards the sky, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) would often raise his head towards the sky, then he said: The stars are a protection for the sky; when the stars disappear, then that which has been promised for the sky will come to it (i.e., the Day of Judgment will come and the sky will be rent asunder and destroyed). And I am a protection for my companions; when I depart, then that which has been promised for my companions will come to them (i.e., tribulations, discord, and fighting). And my companions are a protection for my Ummah; when my companions depart, then that which has been promised for my Ummah will come to them (i.e., differences, disunity, etc.)."
"1742","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon the people when groups of men will go out for jihad, and they will be asked: 'Is there anyone among you who has seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?' They will reply: 'Yes!' So they will be granted victory. Then groups of people will go out for jihad, and they will be asked: 'Is there anyone among you who has seen a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?' (i.e., is there anyone among the Tabi'in?) The people will say: 'Yes!' Then they will be granted victory. Then armies of men will go out for jihad, and they will be asked: 'Is there anyone among you who has seen someone who saw a companion?' (i.e., among the Tabi' Tabi'in?) The people will say: 'Yes.' Then groups of people will go out for jihad, and they will be asked: 'Is there anyone among you who has seen the followers of the followers?'"""
"1743","Narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are those of my generation, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned two generations after his own or three. Then after them there will come people who will bear witness without being asked, will be treacherous and not trustworthy, will make vows but not fulfill them, and obesity will become widespread among them."
"1744","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (Just as some mines are of gold and some of iron, likewise people are also different; some have noble lineage and origin, some are good and some are bad.) You will find people like mines. So those who were better in the time of ignorance are better in Islam as well, when they gain understanding in religion. And you will find the best among you is the one who used to hate Islam the most before becoming Muslim (meaning, the one who was strong in disbelief, after accepting Islam, will be equally strong in Islam, like Sayyiduna Umar and Sayyiduna Khalid bin Walid, may Allah be pleased with them, etc., or it means that the one who dislikes leadership, his leadership will be the best). And you will find the worst among you is the one who is two-faced, who comes to some people with one face and goes to others with another face."
"1745","`Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the Isha prayer one night during the last part of his life. When he finished the prayer with salam, he stood up and said: ""Did you see this night of yours? At the end of a hundred years from now, none of those who are on the earth will remain."" Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said that people make a mistake regarding the hadiths mentioning ""a hundred years."" Rather, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said that none of those present today will remain, meaning this century will be completed."
"1746","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not speak ill of my companions, do not speak ill of my companions. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, if any one of you were to spend gold equal to (the mountain of) Uhud (in the way of Allah), it would not equal a mudd (a handful) or even half a mudd of what they gave."
"1747","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Among the Tabi‘in, there is a best person whose name is Uwais. He has a mother (meaning, among his relatives, only his mother will be alive) and he will have a whiteness (i.e., a skin condition). You should ask him to pray for you."
"1748","Sayyiduna Usayr bin Jabir says that when people came to Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) from Yemen for help (that is, those who came from every country to join the Islamic army for jihad), he would ask them, ""Is there anyone among you named Uwais bin Amir?"" Until Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) himself came to Uwais and asked, ""Is your name Uwais bin Amir?"" He replied, ""Yes."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""Are you from the branch of Qarn of the Murad tribe?"" He replied, ""Yes."" He asked, ""Did you have leucoderma which has been cured except for a spot the size of a dirham?"" He replied, ""Yes."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""Do you have a mother?"" He replied, ""Yes."" Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Uwais bin Amir will come to you with the auxiliary army of the people of Yemen. He is from the Murad tribe, from the branch of Qarn. He had leucoderma which has been cured except for a spot the size of a dirham. He has a mother. His condition is such that if he swears by Allah, Allah will fulfill it. So if you are able, ask him to pray for you.' So pray for me."" Thus, Uwais prayed for Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) for forgiveness. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""Where do you intend to go?"" He replied, ""To Kufa."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Shall I write a letter for you to the governor of Kufa?"" He replied, ""I prefer to remain among the humble."" When the next year came, a person from among the chiefs of Kufa performed Hajj. He met Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who asked him about Uwais. He replied, ""I left Uwais in such a state that there were few possessions in his house and he was in straitened circumstances."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Uwais bin Amir will come to you with the auxiliary army of the people of Yemen. He is from the branch of Qarn of the Murad tribe. He had leucoderma which has been cured except for a spot the size of a dirham. He has a mother with whom he is dutiful. If he swears by Allah, Allah will fulfill it. So if you are able, ask him to pray for you.'"" Upon hearing this, that person went to Uwais and said, ""Pray for me."" Uwais replied, ""You have just returned from a righteous journey (i.e., Hajj), so pray for me."" Then the person said, ""Pray for me."" Uwais gave the same reply. Then he asked, ""Did you meet Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)?"" The person replied, ""Yes, I met him."" Uwais then prayed for him. At that time, people understood the status of Uwais. He then left from there. Usayr said, ""I gave him a cloak to wear. Whenever anyone saw him, they would say, 'Where did Uwais get this cloak from?'"""
"1749","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will conquer a land called Egypt where the unit of currency will be the qirat (qirat is a piece of dirham and dinar, and it was widely used in Egypt). Treat its people well, for they have a covenant and kinship with you (because Lady Hajar, the mother of Isma'il, was from Egypt, and she is the mother of the Arabs) { یا یہ فرمایا کہ ان کا تم پر حق ہے اور ان سے دامادی کا رشتہ بھی ہے } (and that relationship was that the mother of the Prophet's son, Sayyiduna Ibrahim, was Maria, who was from Egypt). So when you see two men fighting over a brick's space there, leave that place."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""I saw that Abdur Rahman bin Shurahbil bin Hasana and his brother Rabee'ah were fighting over a brick's space, so I left that place."""
"1750","Sayyiduna Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a man to a certain tribe of the Arabs. The people there spoke ill of him and beat him. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and related what had happened. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If you had gone to the people of Oman, they would not have spoken ill of you nor beaten you (because the people there are good)."""
"1751","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when Surah Al-Jumu’ah was revealed. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: “Glory be to Allah Who sent a Messenger among the unlettered (Arabs) and among others who have not yet joined them” (Al-Jumu’ah: 3), a man asked, “O Messenger of Allah! Who are these people other than the Arabs?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not answer him until he asked once, twice, or three times. At that time, Sayyiduna Salman Al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) was also sitting among us. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his blessed hand on him and said, “If faith were at Thurayya (the Pleiades, a star), even then some men from his people would attain it.”"
"1752","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will find people like a hundred camels, among which not even one is fit (skilled and excellent) for riding. (In the same way, among a hundred people, you will hardly find one who is excellent, refined, wise, virtuous, fortunate, good-mannered, righteous, pious, or a true monotheist and religious person.)"""
"1753","Abu Nofal says: I saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) at the pass of Madinah (that is, the pass of Makkah which is on the way to Madinah). He says that the people of Quraysh would pass by him and other people as well (Hajjaj had crucified him and left him there), until Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) also passed by him. He stood there and said: ""Peace be upon you, O Abu Khubaib!"" (Abu Khubaib is the kunyah of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair, and Abu Bakr and Abu Bukair are also his kunyahs). ""Peace be upon you, O Abu Khubaib! Peace be upon you, O Abu Khubaib!"" (From this it is understood that saying salam to the deceased three times is recommended). ""By Allah, I used to forbid you from this. By Allah, I used to forbid you from this. By Allah, I used to forbid you from this."" (That is, from taking up the caliphate and government). ""By Allah, as far as I know, you were one who fasted, prayed at night, and maintained ties of kinship. By Allah, the group of which you are considered bad is indeed an excellent group."" (He said this in irony, meaning it is actually a bad group, and in another narration it is clearly stated that it is a bad group). Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) left from there. Then the news of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) standing there and speaking reached Hajjaj, so he had him taken down from the cross and thrown into the Jewish cemetery. (And Hajjaj did not understand what difference this would make. Wherever a person falls, it is necessary that his deeds are good). Then Hajjaj sent for his mother, Sayyidah Asma bint Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both), but she refused to come to Hajjaj. Hajjaj sent again and said: ""If you wish, come; otherwise, I will send someone who will grab you by your hair and drag you here."" She still refused to come and said: ""By Allah, I will not come to you unless you send the one who will drag me by my hair to you."" Finally, Hajjaj said: ""Bring me my shoes,"" and putting on his shoes arrogantly, he went until he reached Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: ""Have you seen what I have done to the enemy of Allah?"" (This Hajjaj said according to his own belief about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair, whereas he himself was the enemy of Allah). Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""I have seen that you have ruined Abdullah bin Zubair's worldly life, and he has ruined your Hereafter. I have heard that you used to call Abdullah bin Zubair 'the son of the woman with two belts'? By Allah, I am indeed the woman with two belts. With one belt, I used to carry food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) so that animals would not eat it, and the other belt was what a woman needs."" (Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) had torn her belt into two pieces: with one she tied her waist, and with the other she made a spread for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). This was the virtue of Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her), which Hajjaj considered a fault and used to call Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair 'the son of the woman with two belts' to humiliate him). ""So beware, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) told us that in Thaqif there would arise a great liar and a great oppressor. We have seen the liar, and as for the oppressor, I do not consider anyone but you."" Hearing this, Hajjaj stood up and gave no reply to Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her)."
